  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1026 PM CST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nThe next mid level trough will take shape over the southwestern U.S. \nSaturday as a low digs into southeast AZ. There is a low chance of \nseeing some light showers across the southern portions of the CWA \nSaturday afternoon however present indications are that these \nshowers should be light and on a downward trend as they come into \nour area. After that system moves by to the south of us we should \nstart to see a warming trend into the early portion of next week \nwith highs getting into the mid 60s. With a benign pattern in place \nit is looking quiet and dry through the early to middle portions of \nnext week.",
